{"title":"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem B","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> be TNYWR.\nIn the diagram, the larger square has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/8/dc8ae3e079c0a8b337c6a3d7abdf751830521959.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2t-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> and the smaller square has side length 4. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_B&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>What is the area of the shaded region?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> of a square is equal to the square of the side length. We can get the area of the shaded region by subtracting the area of the smaller square from the area of the larger <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square\" title=\"Square\">square</a>.\n</p><p>From the diagram, we can see that the small square would have an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e9136809f832318fdd66a5180d0e20660e072b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{2} = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>The larger square would have an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/17903da3a948e86a7a24bc457c3a037c3f7b8a42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2t - 4)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"21\" />. This means that the shaded region would have an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/2/1a240792c8af5d76198d59d973c5bb3fcc2b2fed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2t - 4)^{2} - 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_A\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem A\">seat A</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5bc2ef78516fb01003693c823d005e12e9c756f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />. Plugging this into our area, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6eb126728312977e0f80937e23f123f84abf556.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2 \\times 5 - 4)^{2} - 16 = (10 - 4)^{2} - 16 = 6^{2} - 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"352\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f0148b512ce2795569a7baa0fc90b5443f845897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=36 - 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a193744b19d26ffd34580219c48ffa0c7a980.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\boxed{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"50\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC\">2017 CEMC CTMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_A\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem A\">Relay 1 Problem A</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_C\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem C\">Relay 1 Problem C</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_1\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 1\">Individual 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Individual 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_3\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 3\">Individual 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_4\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 4\">Individual 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=